## 3. Typography Classes

These are **not** in Vuetify's type scale. Define once in `src/assets/typography.css` and import globally in `main.ts`.

```css
/* src/assets/typography.css */
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Barlow+Condensed:wght@400;600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;600&display=swap');

.fc-timer        { font: 600 72px/80px 'JetBrains Mono'; letter-spacing: -2px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.fc-exercise     { font: 700 32px/40px 'Barlow Condensed'; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-transform: uppercase; }
.fc-rep-target   { font: 600 48px/56px 'JetBrains Mono'; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.fc-section      { font: 600 20px/24px 'Barlow Condensed'; letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase; }
.fc-body-lg      { font: 400 18px/28px 'Inter'; }
.fc-body         { font: 400 16px/24px 'Inter'; }
.fc-body-strong  { font: 600 16px/24px 'Inter'; }
.fc-caption      { font: 400 13px/18px 'Inter'; color: rgb(var(--v-theme-on-surface-3)); }
```

**Usage rule:** Use `class="fc-timer text-primary"` — the `fc-*` class controls font; the Vuetify `text-*` class controls colour. Never combine both in a single custom class.

